---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
  business,
  marketingAvailability,
  marketingPrograms,
  noticeVersions,
  providers,
  retentionPolicy,
  trackingPreferences,
} from '../data/business';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Sapphire Blue handles business inquiries, website information and optional tracking, and what is planned for email and SMS."
  version={noticeVersions.privacy}
>
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {business.brand} is operated by {business.operator}, {business.operatorDescription}.
    For privacy questions or requests, email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> and address your request to Asor.
    This site is intended for {business.initialAudience}.
  </p>
  <p>
    On {business.brand}'s side, access to inquiry and client information is limited to {business.authorizedAccess.people} authorized people,
    located in the {business.authorizedAccess.countries[0]} and the {business.authorizedAccess.countries[1]}.
    The service providers below also process information as part of their services.
  </p>

  <h2>Information and purposes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Inquiries:</strong> your name, email address, optional phone number, business name, selected services and anything you choose to include in your message. We use these details to respond, discuss a potential engagement and manage the resulting business relationship.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct correspondence and client records:</strong> information you provide by email or during an engagement, used for the correspondence, agreed services and relevant business records.</li>
    <li><strong>Website delivery:</strong> technical connection and request information processed by the hosting provider to serve the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Browser preferences:</strong> your choices about optional analytics and advertising tools, stored locally as explained below.</li>
    <li><strong>Optional measurement:</strong> page, interaction, technical and performance information processed by the tools you allow. These tools are separate from submitting an inquiry.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please do not put passwords, payment-card details, sensitive personal information or information about children in the inquiry form.
    The site is not directed to children. Providing an email address or phone number for a business inquiry does not enroll you in marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Providers: active, optional and planned</h2>
  <dl class="details-list">
    {Object.values(providers).map(provider => (
      <div>
        <dt>{provider.name}</dt>
        <dd class="status">{provider.status}</dd>
        <dd>{provider.purpose}</dd>
        <dd><strong>Information involved:</strong> {provider.information}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>
  <p>
    The contact flow sends requests to Google Apps Script for handling in Google Sheets and email notification through MailApp.
    Brevo is not part of the current contact flow. It is a proposed provider, not an active email or SMS integration.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional analytics, advertising and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    Use <strong>Privacy settings</strong> in the footer to allow or reject analytics and advertising separately, or to change your choices later.
    Optional tools remain off until the relevant permission is given. Rejecting them does not prevent you from reading the site or making an inquiry.
    These optional tools are not enabled when JavaScript is off, in local development or on preview deployments.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Google Analytics, Vercel Web Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising:</strong> Meta Pixel for advertising measurement.</li>
    <li><strong>Global Privacy Control (GPC):</strong> a detected GPC signal is treated as an objection to advertising tracking. It does not automatically reject analytics, which has its own separate choice.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your browser's <code>localStorage</code> holds these preferences under <code>{trackingPreferences.key}</code>,
    using version {trackingPreferences.version} with a {trackingPreferences.ttlDays}-day validity period.
    The choice belongs to that browser and device. Clearing local storage removes the saved choice; without a valid choice, optional tools stay off unless you allow them.
    This local preference is not a central, verifiable record of email or SMS marketing permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    Changing a preference stops future optional collection by the affected tools on this site; it does not undo information already sent to a provider.
    Measurement may also be suppressed for safety, including on URLs that could expose personal or sensitive information.
    Not every visit or interaction is necessarily measured.
  </p>

  <h2>Email and SMS marketing are not active</h2>
  <div class="notice">
    <p><strong>Current availability:</strong> marketing email is {marketingAvailability.email ? 'enabled' : 'disabled'}; automated marketing SMS is {marketingAvailability.sms ? 'enabled' : 'disabled'}.</p>
    <p>A verifiable marketing-permission register has not been implemented. Neither planned program is accepting subscriptions through this site.</p>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Planned email:</strong> {marketingPrograms.email.purpose} Intended frequency: {marketingPrograms.email.frequency.toLowerCase()}</li>
    <li><strong>Planned SMS:</strong> {marketingPrograms.sms.purpose} {marketingPrograms.sms.frequency} {marketingPrograms.sms.charges}</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Both would use {providers.marketing.name} only after setup and verification. Each channel would require its own optional choice;
    neither would be required to send an inquiry, receive a quote or purchase services.
    A business reply to your request is different from a marketing subscription.
    See the <a href="/sms-terms">planned SMS terms</a> for program limitations and the intended opt-out process.
  </p>

  <h2>Intended retention</h2>
  <p>These are the intended retention targets for records held by {business.brand}:</p>
  <dl class="details-list">
    {Object.values(retentionPolicy).map(item => (
      <div><dt>{item.record}</dt><dd>{item.period}</dd></div>
    ))}
  </dl>
  <p>
    These targets are not a promise of automatic deletion: a deletion schedule has not been implemented.
    Manual review is needed to apply them. Specific record-preservation obligations, disputes, backups and provider-held copies may affect what can be deleted and when.
    Minimal permission or opt-out records would be kept separately from marketing contact lists so an opt-out can continue to be honored.
  </p>

  <h2>Access across countries and provider handling</h2>
  <p>
    Information may be accessed from the Dominican Republic and the United States by the two authorized people described above.
    Service providers may process information in other countries, depending on their services and configuration.
    This notice does not assert a particular cross-border transfer mechanism, certification, provider-account setting or guaranteed processing location.
  </p>
  <p>
    Information may also need to be disclosed in response to an applicable legal obligation or a specific legal claim.
    No online transmission or storage system is risk-free.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your location and the rules that apply, you may have rights to request access, correction or deletion,
    obtain a copy of information, object to or restrict certain uses, withdraw optional permission, or contact a relevant privacy authority.
    Those rights and any exceptions depend on the applicable rules; this notice does not promise a universal set of rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> with your request and enough context to identify the relevant correspondence or records.
    {business.operator} handles requests manually and may ask for information reasonably needed to verify the request.
    Do not send sensitive identity documents unless specifically requested through an appropriate process.
    No fixed response time is stated here; applicable response requirements still apply where relevant.
  </p>
  <p>
    For browser tracking, use the footer's Privacy settings. For an objection to advertising, you can also use a supported GPC signal.
    For questions about the planned marketing programs or information already provided, contact Asor by email rather than relying on an unconfigured SMS command or unsubscribe workflow.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    This notice may be updated when practices or available features change. The date and version above identify this edition.
    Publishing a new notice does not itself enroll you in marketing or replace a separate optional permission.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
